            <ArticleTitle>Prevention of vasospastic angina by alcohol ingestion: report of 2 cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-400</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report 2 patients with vasospastic angina in whom alcohol ingestion was effective in preventing angina. Coronary angiography revealed no organic coronary stenosis but demonstrated coronary artery spasm during angina attacks. In 1 patient, alcohol ingestion every six hours completely suppressed frequent spontaneous angina. In the other patient, alcohol ingestion markedly prolonged the duration of the exercise on treadmill testing by preventing exercise-induced coronary spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
